red pawn on the  queen side  white slight square bishop is attacked  so it has to move this bishop  in the game her opponent continued with  the move bishop to b5  and now the following sequence happened  queen to h4  f3  and now bishop to f5 hitting the rook  white responded with the  counter-attacking move bishop to even  but after queen to f6 it is very obvious  that  white has to move the rook  in the game he continued with the move  rook to c1  but then comes this double attack  so white response is force white has to  block the check with the moon knight to  d4  which at first sight saving everything  but after black's next amazing reply  knight catches f3 check  i think game is already gone  well white doesn't have any good choice  in the game why decided to play  g captures f3 but after bishop captures  d4 check  king to g2  and bishop to e3  black is indeed threatening a piece  well again white doesn't have any good  choices in the game he played  rook to c3 but after queen captures rook  captures  one move and white resigned  can you spot this move  well i hope you find this wonderful blow  bam  so a deflection move which wins the  white rook and in fact the game  well i hope you enjoy and learn this  wonderful queen sacrifice line in the  greenfield exchange edition  feel free to like subscribe and comment  on my video and i'll meet you in my next  episode very soon  bye and take care

